Falsifies `entropy_contract::verification::a_request_word_carries_its_opcode_and_clamped_count`.

The defect: `request` forgets to clamp the byte count. A count above `MAXIMUM_BYTES` then reaches
the wire as it came, and a request for 256 bytes reads back as a request for none, so a client
asking for more than one reply holds is not answered with a full reply.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!` on `operation` or on `requested_bytes`, with any byte count above
`MAXIMUM_BYTES`.
diff --git a/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/entropy_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -70,10 +70,5 @@ pub const GET: u64 = 1;
 /// Name: ratified 2026-11-11 (#3480): renamed from `req`, which abbreviates it.
 pub const fn request(operation: u64, byte_count: u64) -> u64 {
-    let clamped = if byte_count > MAXIMUM_BYTES {
-        MAXIMUM_BYTES
-    } else {
-        byte_count
-    };
-    (operation << OPERATION_SHIFT) | clamped
+    (operation << OPERATION_SHIFT) | byte_count
 }
 
